# Error log + feature docs

## On ANY error

When any error occurs (build, runtime, test, API, tool failure, crash, or user-reported bug), **append one line** to:

`youtube-jp-caption-studio/local-bridge/errors.log`

Match the bridge logger format from `local-bridge/app/main.py` (`logging.basicConfig` default):

```text
ERROR:bridge:<short message>
WARNING:bridge:<short message>
```

Examples:

```text
ERROR:bridge:iPad hardsub popup disappears before next cue at 0:13
ERROR:bridge:scripts/save failed
WARNING:bridge:Sudachi unavailable: no module named sudachipy
```

Rules:

- One line per distinct error; no JSON, no extra timestamp prefix (main logger has none).
- Keep the message concrete (what failed + where).
- Append only — do not rewrite the whole file for a single new error.
- Still fix the error; logging does not replace the fix.

## On new features

When you add a user-facing feature, update both:

1. `youtube-jp-caption-studio/walkthrough.md` — what was added and how to try it
2. `youtube-jp-caption-studio/README.md` — short discovery blurb if the feature should be findable from the README

Skip doc updates for pure bugfixes, renames, or internal refactors with no new capability.
